BLOCKS = [
('W1 Images', '''<ul><li>img[v,u] = [row, col]; origin top-left; uint8 0–255.</li><li>Chromaticity r = R/(R+G+B) (white ≈ 0.33).</li><li>Central diff: f′ ≈ (f(x+ε) − f(x−ε))/2ε; Iₓ kernel [−½ 0 ½].</li><li>∇I = (Iₓ, I_y); |∇I| = √(Iₓ²+I_y²); θ = atan2(I_y, Iₓ) ⟂ edge. Smooth first: ∂(I∗H) = I∗∂H.</li></ul>'''),
('W2 Features', '''<ul><li>Good feature: distinctive, repeatable, well localised.</li><li>Harris A = w∗[Jᵤ² JᵤJᵥ; JᵤJᵥ Jᵥ²]: λ₁,λ₂ large = corner; one large = edge; both small = flat.</li><li>Moravec: min SSD over shifts (fails on diagonal edges).</li><li>SIFT: DoG D = L(kσ) − L(σ); extrema vs 26 neighbours; orientation histogram; 4×4×8 = 128-D.</li><li>BRIEF: random pair tests → 256 bits; Hamming; not rot/scale invariant. ORB = oFAST (pyramid, Harris score, intensity-centroid angle) + rBRIEF.</li><li>FAST: N ≥ 12 contiguous of 16 brighter/darker than I(p) ± t; quick test 1,5,9,13 (≥ 3 of 4).</li><li>Ratio test d₁/d₂ &lt; θ (strict). Cross-check = mutual NN. Euclid for float, Hamming for binary.</li><li>Baseline: ORB + Hamming + ratio/cross-check → RANSAC. SIFT for big scale/viewpoint change.</li><li>SuperGlue: self + cross attention GNN (9 layers) → score matrix + dustbin → Sinkhorn (OT). AUC@20 36.4 → 51.8, precision 50.4 → 84.4%. LightGlue: adaptive depth (early exit) + width (prune points); 44 ms vs 70 ms (adaptive 31 ms).</li></ul>'''),
('W3 Camera & stereo', '''<ul><li>x = fX/Z; u = f·X/Z + u₀ (f in px = f_mm/pixel size). K = [f 0 u₀; 0 f v₀; 0 0 1].</li><li>p̃ = K[R|t]P; C 3×4, scale-free → 11 DOF. Pose (R,t) of camera → extrinsic is its inverse.</li><li>Lost: depth, lengths, angles, parallelism. Kept: straight lines. Vanishing points/lines.</li><li>Thin lens 1/f = 1/Z + 1/e; blur R = Lδ/2e; Z ≫ f → pinhole.</li><li>Bayer RGGB (2× green). Global vs rolling shutter (skew).</li><li><b>Z = fb/d</b>, X = Z(u−u₀)/f, Y = Z(v−v₀)/f; δZ ≈ Z²δd/(fb); Zmin = fb/d_max.</li><li>Big baseline: ↓δZ, ↑Zmin, harder close search. Rectify → search same row.</li><li>Plane → homography H (8 DOF, 4 pts, DLT + SVD).</li></ul>'''),
('W4 Epipolar & RANSAC', '''<ul><li>x′ᵀFx = 0, l′ = Fx; F rank 2, 7 DOF; 8-pt: Af = 0, SVD, force rank 2, normalise.</li><li>Epipole = other camera centre’s image; all epipolar lines pass through it.</li><li>Degenerate: pure rotation, planar scene, collinear points; near: small baseline, far points, forward motion.</li><li>x̂ = K⁻¹x; x̂′ᵀEx̂ = 0; <b>E = K′ᵀFK = [t]ₓR</b>; 5 DOF, ≥ 5 pts; 4 (R,t) → cheirality picks 1; t only up to scale.</li><li><b>k = log(1−p)/log(1−wⁿ)</b>. w=.5,p=.99: n=8 → 1177; 5 → 146; 3 → 35. w=.9,n=8,p=.999 → 13.</li><li>Raising threshold: old inliers stay, outliers may join.</li><li>Variants: PROSAC, LO-RANSAC, MAGSAC++, GC-, USAC.</li></ul>'''),
('W5 Visual odometry', '''<ul><li>Scale ambiguity: K(R·sX + s·t) = s·K(RX + t). Fix with known 3D: s* = argmin Σ‖x − π(K(Rp + st))‖².</li><li>PnP: 1 pt ∞, 2 pts ∞ (bounded), <b>P3P ≤ 4 solutions</b> (+1 pt), ≥ 4 EPnP. Pipeline: P3P + RANSAC → LM refine on inliers.</li><li>Residual = obs − pred; inlier if ‖r‖ &lt; τ (norm, not squared).</li><li>3D–3D (Arun): centroids; H = Σ x̄ₜ₋₁x̄ₜᵀ; USVᵀ = svd(H); R = VUᵀ; t = x̄ₜ − R x̄ₜ₋₁. Less accurate (stereo depth error).</li><li><b>ᴬT_C = ᴬT_B ᴮT_C</b>; C_k = C_{k−1}T_k; ᴮT_A = (ᴬT_B)⁻¹.</li><li>Keyframes: motion threshold, lost features, time; mono: baseline/avg depth &gt; 10–20%.</li><li>Optimisation template: parameters / prediction / residual / objective. Exact → solve; linear → QR/SVD; nonlinear → GN/LM; outliers → robust/RANSAC.</li></ul>'''),
('W6 Graphs & BA', '''<ul><li>Pose graph: X* = argmin Σ‖xᵢ − ⁱTⱼxⱼ‖²_Σ (poses only, relative-pose factors). BA: argmin Σ‖yⱼⁱ − π(pⱼ, xᵢ, K)‖² (poses + landmarks, reprojection).</li><li>Weight 1/σ²: σ halves → 4× influence.</li><li>GN: JᵀJΔx = −Jᵀr; LM: (JᵀJ + λI)Δx = −Jᵀr. Sparse normal equations. Needs a good initial guess (local minima).</li><li>Robust: quadratic (unbounded); L1, Huber k = 1.345 (bounded); Tukey 4.685, Cauchy (redescending); Tukey/Hampel zero influence beyond cut-off.</li><li>Factor graph: bipartite, undirected; variables + factors. Joint = Π factors.</li><li>Gaussian fusion: μ = (μ₁/σ₁² + μ₂/σ₂²)/(1/σ₁² + 1/σ₂²), σ² = 1/(Σ1/σᵢ²).</li><li><b>MAP + Gaussian = weighted nonlinear LS</b> (log, drop const, Mahalanobis eᵀΣ⁻¹e). MAP loses spread.</li></ul>'''),
('W7 SLAM / VIO / eval', '''<ul><li>Direct: photometric error, dense/semi-dense, sub-pixel, needs good init, illumination-sensitive (DSO, DTAM, LSD). Indirect: reprojection, sparse, wide basin (ORB-SLAM, PTAM).</li><li>IMU: gyro ω + accel a; ã = R(a − g) + b + n; bias → error ½bt² (0.05 m/s², 10 s → 2.5 m). Camera bounds drift; IMU gives scale, robustness, 1–10 kHz.</li><li>ATE: align (R,T,s), RMSE of positions (global). RPE: relative-motion error (local drift). Report the median too.</li><li>SLAM = VO + map + loop closure (global consistency). MonoSLAM (EKF), KinectFusion (TSDF), SemanticFusion, SLAM++, QuadricSLAM.</li><li>ORB-SLAM3: tracking, local mapping (local BA), loop & map merging (DBoW2, pose graph, full BA), Atlas. Relocalise = lost; loop = same map; merge = other map.</li></ul>'''),
('W8 Deep learning', '''<ul><li>Task → output / supervision / loss / metric: cls (CE, acc); sem-seg (pixel CE, mIoU); det (cls + box, AP@IoU); inst-seg (mask AP); depth (L2, RMSE); retrieval (contrastive, R@K); obstacle (BCE, P/R at threshold).</li><li>Backbone → embedding → head. Transfer ladder: feature reuse → linear probe → partial FT → full FT → scratch.</li><li>Train / val (tune) / test (once). Loss ≠ metric.</li><li>SSL: contrastive / triplet, MAE, DINO (student–teacher), CLIP.</li><li>CNN: weight sharing, equivariant (not invariant). ViT: N = HW/P², [class] token, position embeddings, softmax(QKᵀ/√d)V, residual. Less inductive bias → needs big data (ViT-H/14 88.55%).</li><li>↓threshold → ↑recall ↑FP; ↑threshold → ↑precision ↑FN. Softmax ≠ calibrated.</li></ul>'''),
('W9 Learned 3D', '''<ul><li>Mono depth: ill-posed, global scale ambiguous. Supervision: direct GT / self-sup photometric (I_L(u,v) vs I_R(u−d,v)) / pseudo-labels (Depth Anything V2: synthetic teacher, 62M images).</li><li>Depth map H×W×1 vs pointmap H×W×3. DUSt3R: pair → 2 pointmaps in cam-1 frame + confidence; up to scale; global alignment (σₑ, Pₑ, Πσ = 1); MASt3R adds descriptors and metric scale.</li><li>Occ-Net f(x,h) → p_occ; DeepSDF → signed distance; NeRF f(x,y,z,θ,φ) → (σ, RGB), volume rendering, no GT geometry; 3DGS: mean, covariance, opacity, SH colour, splat. LERF/LangSplat + CLIP.</li><li>Pretty renders ≠ validated occupancy.</li></ul>'''),
('W10 Detection', '''<ul><li>Variable output count. Two-stage (anchors 3×3, RPN objectness, top-N, RoI pool, head); one-stage anchor (SSD, RetinaNet) / point (FCOS centerness, YOLO); DETR (queries, Hungarian, no NMS).</li><li>Losses: CE/BCE/focal + L1/GIoU (+ objectness). Imbalance: focal, sampling, 1-to-1 matching.</li><li><b>IoU = I/(A + B − I)</b>. TP: IoU ≥ τ, right class, GT not already matched. P = TP/(TP+FP); R = TP/(TP+FN).</li><li>AP = area under PR (monotone envelope, 101 pts); mAP = mean over classes (COCO also over IoU .5:.95). AP ≠ precision at the deployed threshold.</li><li>Closed / open set / open vocabulary (CLIP, Grounding DINO); prompts matter; ≠ reasoning.</li><li>DETR: 42.0 AP = FRCNN-FPN+; APL +7.8, APS −5.5; 100 queries; slow training.</li></ul>'''),
('W11 Seg & grasp', '''<ul><li>Semantic (class per pixel) vs instance (mask per object). C logits/pixel; softmax (exclusive) vs sigmoid.</li><li>Encoder–decoder; pooling / strided conv ↓, unpool / transposed conv ↑; U-Net skips keep boundaries. Mask IoU = |P∩G|/|P∪G|.</li><li>Imbalance: all-background → high accuracy, obstacle IoU 0.</li><li>Grasp planar (x,y,θ,w,q); 6-DoF (x,y,z,φ,θ,ψ,w,q). Generative (GG-CNN per pixel, detection-style) vs discriminative (Dex-Net, slow). Diffusion: grasp distribution. Task-aware: language (GraspMolmo, GraspVLA).</li><li>Contact-GraspNet: contacts in scene cloud, 4-DoF (a, b, w); 17.7M sim grasps; 90.2% vs 80.4%.</li></ul>'''),
('W12 Place recognition', '''<ul><li>VPR = image retrieval (not classification): loop closure, kidnapped robot, PnP candidates.</li><li>Similarity matrix + threshold; single vs multi-session; challenges: viewpoint, illumination, season, dynamics, aliasing.</li><li>P = TP/(TP+FP); R = TP/GTP; F1 = 2PR/(P+R); max recall @100% P; AUPRC; <b>R@K</b> = share of queries with a correct match in the top K.</li><li>Global (compact, fast) vs local (robust, costly). BoW + TF-IDF t = (n_id/n_d)·log(N/n_i). NetVLAD; AnyLoc: DINOv2 + GeM/VLAD, domain vocabularies, up to 4× R@1.</li><li>cos = qᵀa/(‖q‖‖a‖). Triplet / contrastive, hard negatives. Verify geometrically or with sequences (SeqSLAM).</li></ul>'''),
('W13 Failure & uncertainty', '''<ul><li>OOD (p_train(x) ≈ 0) vs open set (new class) vs open world (learn new). Covariate p(x); label p(y); concept p(y|x); novel class.</li><li>Calibrated: n% confidence → n% correct. Bin: acc &lt; conf → over-confident. ECE = Σ(n_b/N)|acc − conf|.</li><li>Temperature: softmax(z/T), T &gt; 1 softens; argmax unchanged; fit on validation.</li><li>Epistemic (reducible with data; ensembles, MC dropout) vs aleatoric (irreducible; L = ‖y−ŷ‖²/2σ² + ½ log σ²). Entropy H = −Σp log p.</li><li>OOD: max softmax, feature distance, energy E = −log Σ e^z. OOD ≠ failure.</li><li>Selective: predict if r(x) &lt; τ. Coverage = predicted/all; risk = wrong/predicted.</li><li>Act on risk: abstain, slow down, re-observe, ask a human. No universal threshold.</li></ul>'''),
('Practice-exam answer key', '''<p>1b 2a 3a 4c 5d 6d 7b 8c 9c 10a · 11b 12c 13b 14c 15d 16a 17a 18a 19d 20b · 21a 22d 23c 24c 25b 26d 27d 28d 29a 30d · 31b 32d 33a 34b 35c 36b 37c 38c 39a 40b</p>'''),
('Practical results (optional, Phase 2)', '''<p>The notebooks have not been run yet, so there are no results of yours to quote. Only the LightGlue demo, Week 5 and Week 6 notebooks contain instructor outputs. This section will be filled in Phase 2.</p>'''),
]
def blocks_html():
    return ''.join(f'<div class="blk"><h4>{t}</h4>{b}</div>' for t, b in BLOCKS)
def render():
    return f'''<section data-panel="cheat" hidden aria-label="Cheatsheet"><div><p class="note mono">Two A4 sides · Unicode maths, matching the PDF</p><h2>Cheatsheet</h2>
<p class="lead">The exam is open book, so this is your fast index: every formula, rule and key number in one place. Whether a separate sheet is allowed doesn’t matter; print it and bring it with your notes.</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap"><button class="btn pri" type="button" data-dl="cheatsheet.pdf">⬇ Download cheatsheet PDF (2 pages A4)</button><a class="btn" href="cheatsheet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open in new tab ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="cheat">{blocks_html()}</div></section>'''
